<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>CSS Fonts, Text & Colors Demo</title>

<style>
  /* Page base styling */
  body {
    background: #0f172a;                 /* Dark blue background */
    color: white;                       /* Default text color */
    font-family: "Poppins", Arial, sans-serif;
    padding: 40px;
  }

  /* Main heading */
  h1 {
    font-size: 42px;                    /* Text size */
    font-weight: 700;                  /* Boldness */
    color: #38bdf8;                    /* Text color */
    text-align: center;                /* Center text */
    text-transform: uppercase;         /* CAPITAL letters */
    letter-spacing: 3px;               /* Space between letters */
    text-shadow: 0 0 15px #38bdf8;       /* Glow effect */
  }

  /* Paragraph */
  p {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-style: oblique;               /* Slanted text */
    line-height: 1.8;                  /* Line gap */
    word-spacing: 5px;                 /* Gap between words */
    color: #e5e7eb;
  }

  /* Highlight text */
  span {
    color: #22c55e;                    /* Green color */
    font-weight: bold;
    text-decoration: underline;       /* Underline */
  }

  /* Box */
  .card {
    background: #020617;
    padding: 25px;
    border: 2px solid #38bdf8;
    border-radius: 10px;
    width: 60%;
    margin: 40px auto;
    box-shadow: 0 0 30px #38bdf8;
  }

  /* Link styling */
  a {
    color: #f97316;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 18px;
  }

  a:hover {
    color: #22c55e;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

</style>
</head>

<body>

  <h1>CSS Fonts, Text & Colors</h1>

  <div class="card">
    <p>
      This is a <span>professional demo</span> showing how
      fonts, colors and text styling work in CSS.
      Everything here is designed to look <span>modern and intuitive</span>.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can upload this project on <a href="#">GitHub</a>
      and use it for learning and practice.
    </p>
  </div>

</body>
</html>
